# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (2026-10-04): the Commodore 64 at BASIC V2 READY ----
# The SECOND C64 in the museum. `c64` boots GEOS and stays that way; this one
# is the machine as it powered on, so the type-in code editor has a C64 to
# type into. Same engine as every converted VICE station: VICE 3.10.0's x64sc
# runs ON THE HOST, headless — no QEMU, no guest OS, no X. Frames VICE_SHM_PATH
# -> SH_CAPTURE=shm; keys the vicectl socket + the ONE shared keysym table
# (VICE resolves keysym -> matrix through C64/gtk3_sym.vkm); audio -sounddev
# fifo -> named FIFO with the daemon as clock. Launcher: the shared
# stations/vice-native/x11-runtime.sh, VICE_NATIVE_* knobs.
# Build + golden: scripts/build-guests/tiles/c64basic.sh all.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore 64 (PAL breadbin, -model c64: 6569 VIC-II, 6581 SID) at its power-on screen — "**** COMMODORE 64 BASIC V2 **** / 64K RAM SYSTEM  38911 BASIC BYTES FREE / READY." in light blue on blue inside a light-blue border — restored from a checkpoint by host-native VICE 3.10.0 x64sc. PUBLISHED SURFACE 768x544, MEASURED off the shm mapping (1 671 232 B = 64 + 768*544*4): the PAL VIC-II screen with normal borders times VICIIDoubleSize, the same surface the c64 station publishes. Nothing is curated and nothing is typed; the checkpoint in sta/golden.vsf is an untouched cold boot. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; SID sound -> FIFO.
# THE SAME BINARY AS c64, byte for byte (tiles/c64basic.sh stage refuses on a
# sha256 mismatch), in this station's OWN asset dir: the launcher's reap sweep
# kills every process whose exe lives under the asset dir, so sharing c64's
# path would kill the GEOS station on every reset of this one.
VICE_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/c64basic/vice-native/bin/x64sc
VICE_NATIVE_DATA=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/c64basic/vice-native/share/vice
# The ONLY thing that decides the published geometry (see SH_FIXTURE_DESC).
# -model c64 is the 1982 breadbin (6569 VIC-II, 6581 SID); x64sc's default is
# the later C64C (8565), which is the wrong machine for this exhibit. No drive
# flags and no disk: the scene is ROM BASIC and nothing loads.
VICE_NATIVE_ARGS=-model c64 -VICIIdsize
SH_VICECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64basic/ctl.sock
SH_VICESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64basic/us-layout.keysyms
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64basic/audio.fifo

# ---- CHECKPOINT: ON ----
# A cold boot would reproduce this scene for free (~2 s to READY), but the
# checkpoint is what a reset restores, and restoring is a cut rather than a
# boot (VICE_SHM_HOLD_RESTORE in the launcher). Baked by tiles/c64basic.sh
# bake: SAVEST at READY on a namespaced rig, restored in a fresh process the
# launcher's way, frame-compared, then renamed into place. It belongs to ONE
# x64sc build and ONE VICE_NATIVE_ARGS: change either and rebake.

# ---- STANDBY (instant-ready: an emulator nobody watches costs ~0 CPU) ----
# The launcher freezes the emulator once the scene has painted; the daemon owns
# it after that (SIGSTOP after the idle grace with zero sessions, unconditional
# SIGCONT the moment a visitor connects). WITHOUT THESE TWO LINES A HOST-NATIVE
# STATION BURNS A FULL CORE AROUND THE CLOCK. _PROC_MATCH is the anti-footgun:
# the signal only ever reaches a pid whose cmdline carries THIS station's own
# asset path — and here it is what keeps a signal meant for c64basic away from
# the c64 station's identical binary. Rollback is one line: SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/c64basic/vice.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/c64basic/vice-native
VICE_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING ----
# 60/60 with EXCL, the VICE floor (vic20's re-bisect: 40/40 corrupted 6 of 12
# overlapping-burst lines, 60/60 0 of 12), RE-MEASURED on this machine rather
# than inherited: see docs/guests/c64basic.md "Keyboard".
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=60
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=60
# SHIFT STAGING (2026-10-04), handed to the module as VICE_CTL_KEY_MOD_LEAD.
# `:` `*` `+` `@` are Shift+key on the visitor's US keyboard but plain keys on a
# C64 (the .vkm's deshift), and `'` `[` `]` are the reverse. VICE used to flip
# SHIFT and set the key in ONE latch of the matrix, and a KERNAL scan straddling
# it read the wrong key — about 1 such character in 20 here, the worst of the
# family (docs/guests/c64basic.md "Keyboard"). The old binary tore 20 lines
# in 3 passes of the 14-line stress listing. With a lead the module presents the
# Shift level the key needs AHEAD of the key: 0 in 3, and the three examples
# 9 of 9, all through the daemon at the editor's pace
# (stations/c64basic/evidence/shift-lead-2026-10-04/). Two frames is safe by
# construction (a VICE key event latches at most ~1 frame + 1,000 cycles after
# its push, so a whole frame separates the two latches); PAL, 19 656 cycles a
# frame, so two frames are 40 ms.
SH_KEY_MOD_LEAD_MS=40
# typeIn.perCharMs / demoProgram.perCharMs (170) stay >= HOLD + max(GAP, LEAD)
# + LEAD = 160. No
# SH_KEY_MAP and no per-station keymap file: VICE's own symbolic keymap does
# that job. A SHIFTED letter on a C64 at power-on is a graphics glyph, which
# registry keyboard.letterCase (upper-only) and typeIn.case (unshifted) declare.
